{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1540721950,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNzQ3MzgxNTY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2955","origin":"github"},"title":"AnnexRepo.add() ignores symlinks on Windows (GitRepo.add() works)","message":"Demo:\n\nThis is a function from datalad-revolution that failed in https://ci.appveyor.com/project/mih/datalad-revolution/builds/19855520 in the analog of this test of `add`: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/84f44bc882f01f4e3a4c28bff92a6cb7e6f1fc69/datalad/distribution/tests/test_add.py#L436\n```\n(Pdb) ds.repo.save()\n*** datalad.support.exceptions.FileNotInRepositoryError: FileNotInRepositoryErro\nr: command '['git', '-c', 'receive.autogc=0', '-c', 'gc.auto=0', 'commit', '-m',\n 'dryrun', '--dry-run', '--no-status', '--', 'symlink']' failed with exitcode 1\nFile(s) unknown to git\n[Errno 1] ['git', '-c', 'receive.autogc=0', '-c', 'gc.auto=0', 'commit', '-m', '\ndryrun', '--dry-run', '--no-status', '--', 'symlink']: File(s) unknown to git: ''\n```\nWe are on windows:\n```\n(Pdb) path\n'C:\\\\Users\\\\appveyor\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\1\\\\datalad_temp_yhax7f_o'\n```\nThe reason is that AnnexRepo.add() simply ignores the presence of the symlink, and does nothing (not error), and subsequently `Repo.commit()` fails, because it tries to commit something that had not been added yet.\n```\n(Pdb) ds.repo.add('symlink')\n[]\n```\nIn contrast, `GitRepo.add()` does the right thing (for this demo, the symlink was unstaged in a separate console session before this next line.\n```\n(Pdb) from datalad .support.gitrepo import GitRepo\n(Pdb) GitRepo.add(ds.repo, files='symlink')\n{'success': True, 'file': 'symlink'}\n```\n\nI am aware that this test is not even considered as part of the -core Windows tests, but -revolution is using this function still, and its failure seems to be the last issues before achieving full symlink capability on windows in -revolution -- hence reporting it here.","files":null}]}